<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Free imperial city</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as free imperial cities, free cities</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A free imperial city was a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> that was subject only to the emperor rather than a territorial prince. Such cities had self-government and representation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperial-diet">Imperial Diet</a>. Most lost their status in the Napoleonic reorganisation, though a few survived as city-states into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/free-imperial-city.jpg" alt="Free imperial city" width="320" height="275" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lubiesque · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Free_Imperial_Cities_1792.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
